    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33219" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκφρων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρήν</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>out of one's mind, beside
				oneself</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				2.117
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nigr.</u>
				38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				2.9.8
			</span></i>; <i>senseless, stupid</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.267
			</span></i>; also, <i>frenzied, enthusiastic</i>, of poets, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ion</u>
				534b
			</span></i>; of Bacchantes, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Bacch.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.220.2
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Diosc.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				790e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φρόνως, ἥττων γίγνεσθαι τῶν
					προσπιπτόντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					6.9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
